[86.222088, "o", "pdftotext music_history/2405.07574v1.pdf - | head -n 20\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[86.276781, "o", "Is it getting harder to make a hit? Evidence from 65"]
[86.277009, "o", "\r\n"]
[86.277234, "o", "years of US music chart history"]
[86.277419, "o", "\r\n"]
[86.277578, "o", "Marta Ewa Lecha , Sune Lehmanna,b , and Jonas L. Juula,b"]
[86.277744, "o", "\r\n"]
[86.277897, "o", "\r\n"]
[86.27807, "o", "arXiv:2405.07574v1 [physics.soc-ph] 13 May 2024"]
[86.278242, "o", "\r\n"]
[86.278511, "o", "\r\n"]
[86.278684, "o", "a Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Technical University of Denmark, DK-2800 Kgs."]
[86.278841, "o", "\r\n"]
[86.278999, "o", "\r\n"]
[86.279149, "o", "Lyngby, Denmark"]
[86.279338, "o", "\r\n"]
[86.279481, "o", "b Copenhagen Center for Social Data Science, University of Copenhagen, DK-1353 Kgs. København K, Denmark"]
[86.279617, "o", "\r\n"]
[86.279718, "o", "\r\n"]
[86.279818, "o", "ABSTRACT"]
[86.279918, "o", "\r\n"]
[86.280008, "o", "Since the creation of the Billboard Hot 100 music chart in 1958, the chart has been a window into"]
[86.280122, "o", "\r\n"]
[86.280206, "o", "the music consumption of Americans. Which songs succeed on the chart is decided by consumption"]
[86.280297, "o", "\r\n"]
[86.280371, "o", "volumes, which can be affected by consumer music taste, and other factors such as advertisement"]
[86.280463, "o", "\r\n"]
[86.280541, "o", "budgets, airplay time, the specifics of ranking algorithms, and more. Since its introduction, the chart has"]
[86.280626, "o", "\r\n"]
[86.280706, "o", "documented music consumerism through eras of globalization, economic growth, and the emergence of"]
[86.280806, "o", "\r\n"]
[86.281073, "o", "new technologies for music listening. In recent years, musicians and other hitmakers have voiced the"]
[86.281258, "o", "ir"]
[86.281384, "o", "\r\n"]
[86.281495, "o", "worry that the music world is changing: Many claim that it is getting harder to make a hit but until now,"]
[86.281618, "o", "\r\n"]
[86.281725, "o", "the claims have not been backed using chart data. Here we show that the dynamics of the Billboard"]
[86.283275, "o", "\r\n"]
[86.286281, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@b4b2e5e10690:~# "]
