[328.50024, "o", "Keywords – cultural evolution, electronic music, phylo\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kgenetics\u001b[m\u001b[K, community detection, horizontal transmission"]
[328.500541, "o", "\r\n"]
[328.500696, "o", "recent advancements in network-based phylo\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kgenetics\u001b[m\u001b[K allow\r\nand similarities in the cultural products of different populations (analogous to differences and similarities in \u001b[01;31m\u001b[KDNA\u001b[m\u001b[K) to\r\n"]
[328.518766, "o", "To measure horizontal transmission between two populations, we divided the total number of weighted links between populations by the sum of the number of inte\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Krna\u001b[m\u001b[Kl"]
[328.518831, "o", "\r\nFuzz, Eruption, Sy & Unknown, \u001b[01;31m\u001b[KDNA\u001b[m\u001b[K, DJ Fade\r\n"]
[328.530885, "o", "the conceptualization of horizontal transmission in biological phylo\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kgenetics\u001b[m\u001b[K. Similarly, we define vertical transmission as cultural transmission occurring within populations.\r\nthe ratio of inte\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Krna\u001b[m\u001b[Kl to exte\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Krna\u001b[m\u001b[Kl links, for each individual\r\n"]
[328.53095, "o", "inte\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Krna\u001b[m\u001b[Kl weighted links from each population.\r\n"]
[328.541983, "o", "is likely due to the fact that exte\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Krna\u001b[m\u001b[Kl connections to other"]
[328.542906, "o", "\r\n"]
[328.550016, "o", "limited to releases tagged as “electronic” on Discogs, so exte\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Krna\u001b[m\u001b[Kl connections to other genres (e.g. rock and pop music)\r\n"]
[328.550554, "o", "heuristic for phylo\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kgenetics\u001b[m\u001b[K? Systematic Biology 63, 628–638 (2014).\r\n"]
[328.551164, "o", "Rivero, D. G. in Cultural Phylo\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kgenetics\u001b[m\u001b[K: Concepts and Applications\r\nPhylo\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kgenetics\u001b[m\u001b[K. Mind and Language 32, 65–100 (2017).\r\n"]
[328.551366, "o", "Te\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Krna\u001b[m\u001b[Kry Rhythm Timelines in Proceedings of BRIDGES: Mathematical Connections in Art, Music and Science (2003), 1–18.\r\nof both vertebrate and invertebrate \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kgenome\u001b[m\u001b[Ks. \u001b[01;31m\u001b[KGenome\u001b[m\u001b[K Biology 16\r\nMusic Performance Analysis. Jou\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Krna\u001b[m\u001b[Kl of New Music Research 41,\r\nBock, R. The give-and-take of \u001b[01;31m\u001b[KDNA\u001b[m\u001b[K: horizontal gene transfer in\r\n"]
[328.560339, "o", "Scapoli, C. et al. Su\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Krna\u001b[m\u001b[Kmes and dialects in France: Population structure and cultural evolution. Jou\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Krna\u001b[m\u001b[Kl of Theoretical Biology 237, 75–\r\nbiological phylogenetic analyses of Turkmen textiles. Jou\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Krna\u001b[m\u001b[Kl of Anthropological Archaeology 21, 443–463 (2002).\r\nJordan, P. & Shennan, S. Cultural transmission, language, and basketry traditions amongst the California Indians. Jou\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Krna\u001b[m\u001b[Kl of Anthropological Archaeology 22, 42–74 (2003).\r\n"]
[328.560407, "o", "Tëmkin, I. & Eldredge, N. Phylo\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kgenetics\u001b[m\u001b[K and material cultural evolution. Current Anthropology 48, 146–153 (2007).\r\nJou\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Krna\u001b[m\u001b[Kl of Popular Music Studies 13, 59–75 (2001).\r\nusing editorial metadata from the Discogs database in 18th Inte\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Krna\u001b[m\u001b[Ktional Society for Music Information Retrieval Conference\r\nare driven by counter-dominance signals of elite competition: Quantitative evidence from music styles. Jou\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Krna\u001b[m\u001b[Kl of the Royal Society\r\nnetwork research. InterJou\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Krna\u001b[m\u001b[Kl Complex Systems, 1695. http :\r\nPamjav, H., Juhász, Z., Zalán, A., Németh, E. & Damdin, B. A comparative phylogenetic study of \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kgenetics\u001b[m\u001b[K and folk music. Molecular\r\n\u001b[01;31m\u001b[KGenetics\u001b[m\u001b[K and Genomics 287, 337–349 (2012).\r\n"]
[328.568753, "o", "Models. Jou\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Krna\u001b[m\u001b[Kl of Statistical Software 40, 1–30 (2011).\r\nof Independent Cultural Production. The British Jou\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Krna\u001b[m\u001b[Kl of Sociology 49, 234–251 (1998).\r\nFormilan, G. & Stark, D. Underground testing: Name-altering practices as probes in electronic music. British Jou\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Krna\u001b[m\u001b[Kl of Sociology,\r\n"]
[328.57428, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@b4b2e5e10690:~# "]
[681.711674, "i", "cat << 'EOF' > classify.py\nimport os, subprocess, zipfile, re\nimport xml.etree.ElementTree as ET\n\ndef get_text(path):\n    if path.endswith('.pdf'):\n        return subprocess.check_output(['pdftotext', path, '-'], stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL).decode('utf-8', errors='ignore')\n    if path.endswith('.docx'):\n        try:\n            with zipfile.ZipFile(path) as z:\n                root = ET.fromstring(z.read('word/document.xml'))\n                return \" \".join(node.text for node in root.iter() if node.text)\n        except: return \"\"\n    if path.endswith('.pptx'):\n        try:\n            text = []\n            with zipfile.ZipFile(path) as z:\n                for f in z.namelist():\n                    if f.startswith('ppt/slides/slide'):\n                        root = ET.fromstring(z.read(f))\n                        text.append(\" \".join(node.text for node in root.iter() if node.text))\n            return \" \".join(text)\n        except: return \"\"\n    return \"\"\n\ndef classify(text, filename):\n    text = text.lower() + \" \" + filename.lower()\n    \n    # Check for Music History first to avoid false positives in others\n    if re.search(r'\\b(music|composer|symphony|jazz|opera|orchestra|rhythm|melody|harmony|billboard|pop music|electronic music)\\b', text):\n        return \"music_history\"\n\n    # Check for Black Hole\n    if re.search(r'\\b(black hole|event horizon|hawking radiation|schwarzschild|general relativity)\\b', text):\n        return \"black_hole\"\n    # Check for DNA\n    if re.search(r'\\b(dna|genome|genetics|sequencing|nucleotide|chromosome|rna)\\b', text):\n        return \"DNA\"\n    # Check for Trapped Ion / QC\n    if re.search(r'\\b(trapped ion|quantum computing|qubit|quantum gate|rydberg|ion trap|quantum simulation)\\b', text):\n        return \"trapped_ion_and_qc\"\n    # Check for LLM\n    if re.search(r'\\b(large language model|llm|transformer|gpt|attention mechanism|pre-training|nlp)\\b', text):\n        return \"LLM\"\n    \n    return \"music_history\"\n\ncats = ['LLM', 'trapped_ion_and_qc', 'black_hole', 'DNA', 'music_history']\nfor c in cats: os.makedirs(c, exist_ok=True)\n\nall_files = []\nfor c in cats:\n    for f in os.listdir(c):\n        all_files.append(os.path.join(c, f))\n\nfor path in all_files:\n    if os.path.isdir(path): continue\n    filename = os.path.basename(path)\n    text = get_text(path)\n    category = classify(text, filename)\n    \n    dest = os.path.join(category, filename)\n    if path != dest:\n        os.rename(path, dest)\nEOF\npython3 classify.py\n"]
